Turnip 26.2.0: the 2-slice Adreno 840 (chip id 0x44050A21).

Retail SM8850 phones report their Adreno 840 as chip id 0x44050A21 (KGSL
gpu_model Adreno840v2). Turnip 26.2.0 lists only 0x44050A31, finds no device
info and refuses the GPU (VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER), so DXVK gets no
Vulkan instance and the game cannot start. Mesa added the id in commit
07ea97900e735afff9bfd59805983912f72f7dfd ("freedreno: add 2 slice Adreno 840
chip id", in 26.3.0-rc2, not on the 26.2 branch).

The app ships the prebuilt usr/lib/libvulkan_freedreno.so of the
turnip-26.2.0 package of Winlator 11.2. That build has its own changes
(window system integration for its X server) whose source is not published
for 26.2.0, so the driver is not rebuilt from Mesa. Instead the device table
entry of the Adreno X2-90 (chip id 0xffff44070041, a laptop part of the
Snapdragon X2 Elite; no Android device has it) becomes the 2-slice 840.
Its device info (__info36) is used by no other entry; it gets the values of
Mesa's new entry, which are the 840's (__info34) with 4 CCUs, 2 slices and a
tile alignment of 64 x 32. Applied by tools/binpatch.py (patch
"turnip-a840v2") when the runtime is built:

  file      usr/lib/libvulkan_freedreno.so
  before    sha256 99fd7b22666c7b0fa4e86ef675300e05115ffd05acc1a3c178d7343daa7e4584
  after     sha256 e9e1dd73e680a5925d10c85a6f7ed3a0d8a888a9dde846ea3f92cf2ac6e34197
  changes   (fd_dev_recs entry 84 at 0xeaec38, __info36 at 0xda6ac8, 0x318 bytes)
  file offset 0x71060: e0 -> b8          name pointer of entry 84, addend of its R_AARCH64_RELATIVE relocation:
                                         "Adreno (TM) X2-90" -> "Adreno (TM) 840" (the string of the 840's entry)
  file offset 0xda6ad0: 40 -> 20         __info36 tile_align_h 64 -> 32
  file offset 0xda6b0c: 08 -> 04         __info36 num_ccu 8 -> 4
  file offset 0xda6b10: 04 -> 02         __info36 num_slices 4 -> 2
  file offset 0xda6dbf: 00 -> 01         __info36 props.shading_rate_matches_vk false -> true
  file offset 0xeaec40: 41 00 07 -> 21 0a 05   chip id of entry 84: 0xffff44070041 -> 0xffff44050a21
  file offset 0xeaec48: e0 -> b8         name pointer of entry 84 in place (same value as the addend)

Checked: Mesa 26.2.0's freedreno_devices.py with the change below, run through
its generator, gives an info for the new entry that is byte for byte the
patched __info36 (struct fd_dev_info of 26.2.0); Winlator's __info34 (840) is
byte for byte upstream's. No other entry, no code and no relocation into the
info structs changes; the X2-90 is not known any more.

The source change it corresponds to (Mesa 26.2.0, the X2-90 entry replaced by
the entry of commit 07ea9790 with the "magic_regs" argument 26.2 requires):

--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
@@ -1459,15 +1459,17 @@
         raw_magic_regs = a8xx_base_raw_magic_regs,
     ))
 
+# 2 slice configuration of a840
 add_gpus([
-        GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44070041, name="Adreno (TM) X2-90"),
+        GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44050A21, name="Adreno (TM) 840"),
     ], A6xxGPUInfo(
         CHIP.A8XX,
-        [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen3, a8xx_base, a8xx_gen2],
-        num_ccu = 8,
-        num_slices = 4,
+        [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen3, a8xx_base, a8xx_gen2,
+         GPUProps(shading_rate_matches_vk = True)],
+        num_ccu = 4,
+        num_slices = 2,
         tile_align_w = 64,
-        tile_align_h = 64,
+        tile_align_h = 32,
         tile_max_w = 16384,
         tile_max_h = 16384,
         num_vsc_pipes = 32,
